<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>decision-brief-brief.md</title><style>body{font:18px system-ui;line-height:1.6;max-width:1000px;margin:2rem auto;padding:1rem;color:#17252d;background:white}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{border-collapse:collapse}td,th{border:1px solid #777;padding:.5rem}a{color:#064b8c}</style><main><h1>Draft a one-page spending decision brief — learner brief</h1>
<p>Fictional Northstar Services training material.</p>
<h2>Approved fictional facts</h2>
<p>F1 September budget USD 200,000.
F2 actual USD 218,000; supplied variance USD 18,000 / 9%.
F3 approved explanation USD 12,000 contractor extension and USD 6,000 travel.
F4 forecast revision proposed, unapproved.
F5 operations lead must confirm remaining contractor end date by September 25.</p>
<h2>Supplied options</h2>
<p>D1 maintain support one month, estimated incremental USD 8,000.
D2 reduce support, estimated two-week delay.
D3 controller recommends D1; CFO decision requested September 26. Neither option approved.
D4 revenue effect unknown. Estimates are fictional writing inputs.</p>
<h2>Task</h2>
<p>Northstar&#39;s controller has already evaluated two responses to a contractor extension. Prepare a brief for the CFO.</p>
<h2>Actions</h2>
<ol>
<li>Identify the approved observations and separately list estimates and unknowns.</li>
<li>Ask AI to propose an outline before drafting.</li>
<li>Draft a brief up to 350 words using only the supplied options and recommendation.</li>
<li>Check that the unknown revenue effect remains explicit and estimates stay labeled.</li>
<li>Prepare a three-sentence oral summary containing the same decision request.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Output</h2>
<p>Headline; facts; supplied options table; recommendation attributed to controller; unknowns; CFO decision request.</p>
</main></html>